  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">High quality cassava flour project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled, because of deterioration of the market perspectives and increasing cost prices.The project will establish a production facility for the processing of fresh cassava into high quality cassava flour (HQCF) that as low cost carbohydrate raw material can be used in several agro-alimentary processes in particular as replacement for imported wheat flour in bakeries, pastry and biscuit making.The project will be implemented by a joint venture of the applicant Les Moulins de la Concorde (LMLC) which is the biggest flour mill in Mauritius and the local partner LFL Madagascar, which is involved amongst other in the manufacturing of animal feed. Although in the past, there has been an experimental processing unit for cassava flour, the quality of the flour was and is unsuitable to be used as replacement in bakeries and pastries for wheat flour.The present project will be able to meet the high quality demand. The production of 2,500 tons HQCF annually will require the supply of 7,500 tons of fresh cassava, produced by more than 2,000 smallholder farmers and collected by 20 collectors. The processing facility will be located in Fianarantsoa, in the heart of the area where there is excess production of cassava according to a detailed study of the World Bank.</narrative>
  </description>
